TITLE:: DeleteCommand
SUMMARY:: Command that deletes selected piano-roll notes.
CATEGORIES:: Commands
RELATED:: Classes/Command, Classes/Parameter, Classes/CommandPrompt, Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/PianoRollNote

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::DeleteCommand:: is a LINK::Classes/Command:: named CODE::delete:: that deletes every note in CODE::selectedNotes::. LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: supplies the notes through LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt#-ambientParameters:: as CODE::selectedNotes::, so the user does not type an argument. After the CODE::delete:: chip is committed, LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt:: treats the command as satisfied. Press Return to execute.

Each note that responds to CODE::delete:: is deleted. LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote#-delete:: removes the note view and runs the note's delete callback, which drops the note from the roll and updates the embedded LINK::Classes/SequencePlayer:: sequence. An empty selection is a no-op.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a new TELETYPE::DeleteCommand::. Takes no arguments; deletion is applied by LINK::#-execute::.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::DeleteCommand:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: execute
Deletes each note in CODE::\selectedNotes:: that responds to CODE::delete::.

ARGUMENT:: args
A LINK::Classes/Dictionary:: or LINK::Classes/Event:: with CODE::\selectedNotes:: (an LINK::Classes/Array:: of notes that respond to CODE::delete::). A missing or empty array deletes nothing.

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
(
var notes = [
	PianoRollNote(0, 60, 100,
		viewFunc: { View() },
		selectFunc: {},
		deselectFunc: {},
		setPart1Func: {},
		setPart2Func: {},
		setPart3Func: {},
		setPart4Func: {},
		moveFunc: {},
		deleteFunc: { |note| ("deleted " ++ note.noteNumber).postln }
	),
	PianoRollNote(1, 64, 100,
		viewFunc: { View() },
		selectFunc: {},
		deselectFunc: {},
		setPart1Func: {},
		setPart2Func: {},
		setPart3Func: {},
		setPart4Func: {},
		moveFunc: {},
		deleteFunc: { |note| ("deleted " ++ note.noteNumber).postln }
	)
];
notes.do({ |note| note.stop(note.startTime + 1.0) });
DeleteCommand.new.execute((selectedNotes: notes));
)
::
